{"title":"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(PIE)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (PIE)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Subtraction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Subtraction)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Venn_Diagrams_and_Algebraic_Substitution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Venn Diagrams and Algebraic Substitution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Overcounting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Overcounting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students participating in an after-school program offering classes in yoga, bridge, and painting. Each student must take at least one of these three classes, but may take two or all three. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students taking yoga, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> taking bridge, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> taking painting. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> students taking at least two classes. How many students are taking all three classes?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/9959d47fffb760b6cf89894df252b99436e4d8f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28PIE.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(PIE)\">Solution 1 (PIE)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (PIE)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=PIE\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"PIE\">PIE</a> (Property of Inclusion/Exclusion), we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e6c135f16c3b87078b7b3ebf9a94584aa103776.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A_1 \\cup A_2 \\cup A_3| = \\sum |A_i| - \\sum |A_i \\cap A_j| + |A_1 \\cap A_2 \\cap A_3|.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"456\" height=\"25\" />\nNumber of people in at least two sets is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/9134ea1870bc94d5621c920293c7e08b1148286a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum |A_i \\cap A_j| - 2|A_1 \\cap A_2 \\cap A_3| = 9.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"280\" height=\"25\" />\nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6e8405bc51e093b67a5c76fb46e4fab01b73754.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 = (10 + 13 + 9) - (9 + 2x) + x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"270\" height=\"18\" /> which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/863e5b74fc23ec6706de7c217601a7f28cbf8b2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"93\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Subtraction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Subtraction)\">Solution 2 (Subtraction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Subtraction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The total number of classes taken among the 20 students is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/37817f63a89ac5e287e3b5d1c3590044188f163e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 + 13 + 9 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" />. Each student is taking at least one class so let's subtract the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> classes ( <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> per each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students) from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> classes to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> classes is the total number of extra classes taken by the students who take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> classes. Since we know that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> students taking at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> classes, there must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9703f84d51fe6736dbd69fe66010ad73530362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 - 9 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"129\" height=\"28\" /> students that are taking all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> classes.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Algebra)\">Solution 3 (Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Total class count is 32. Assume there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> students taking one class, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> students taking two classes, ad <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> students taking three classes. Because there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students total, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356c83a2c1c4aafd0eed88bf7e0264380282d43b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />. Because each student taking two classes is counted twice, and each student taking three classes is counted thrice in the total class count, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e76df7c51b5170e1e1990611a8df26c4e32ba092.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+2b+3c = 10+13+9 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"244\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> students taking two or three classes, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/9/fb90865a180773d762ee167d6cc860297a283d1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />. Solving this system of equations gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4a027c1b4ed7258924a91ee12810051884ff6d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) 3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"88\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Venn_Diagrams_and_Algebraic_Substitution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Venn_Diagrams_and_Algebraic_Substitution)\">Solution 4 (Venn Diagrams and Algebraic Substitution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Venn Diagrams and Algebraic Substitution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us assign the following variables and put them in our Venn Diagram<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/File:IMG_20220704_192122676_2.jpg#filelinks\">[1]</a>:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> which designates the number of people taking exactly Bridge and Yoga.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> which designates the number of people taking exactly Bridge and Painting.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> which designates the number of people that took all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> classes or what we want to find.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> which designates the number of people taking exactly Yoga and Painting.\n</p><p>Let's now recall what information we have given: There are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people that are taking at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> classes meaning in other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people total are taking strictly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> classes or strictly all the available classes meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/b/32bbce32e0ccae1a591ac7a2225e3b98c559562b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let's now start filling out the Venn Diagram:\nStrictly taking Bridge, no other classes: We know in total, the number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, however this includes the people taking other classes too meaning we'd need to do some subtraction. From our Venn Diagram we see that we'd need to subtract the following variables to get our wanted outcome here, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. Giving our answer as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca9d8c7a2985029704a2b68c9bf690d15a0ad30c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13-(a+b+c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>However, this equation seems complicated as it has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different variables, so to make this look a lot less complicated we can use our earlier equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/b/32bbce32e0ccae1a591ac7a2225e3b98c559562b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" /> to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddfd701c3467148123a1aaefc65fe7805db142c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=9-d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" />. This means that this can also be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/d/f2dda0d27d4b2a1418d8eed002322efd6d8d3974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13-(9-d)=4+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nStrictly taking Yoga Only: The total number of people is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, but this would also count people taking other classes too along with it, so we need to subtract this overcount which is visible in the Venn Diagram giving us: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2ed2cfad4056d580b92077cd5f684c6e99324575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-(a+c+d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Again, we can use substitution to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fca005de7b6753fe6c0599e99254a84f02194ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+c+d=9-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" />. This simplifies our equation to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/7/e67b73771f2f5ed8eb3d5c8f9e09a9789987136e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-(9-b)=1+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Strictly taking Painting Only: We know again, in total this number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which also accounts for the people taking other classes too. From our Venn Diagram it is visible that we need to subtract: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b935c15651d822aa87116a2c254e1a1ff73de233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f87cb66f758667cec1f8567c573480293c132a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-(b+c+d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Again, through substitution of our first equation we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/852aff1989408acf88ae18a35c84e63eebc6fa4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c+d=9-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" /> meaning we can simplify this equation to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1b334f3f24dfab0f273e909f920f6e5b31354c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-(9-a)=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIf we add these newly made equations of strictly taking one class, we get the total number of people taking exactly one class as these equations each were a subcase for it. We can also find the exact number for this because we are given that there are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students in total, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> students are taking exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> classes, meaning that if we do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64a2fe317c722c132b27473b618f8527bba33968.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> we get our answer for the number of students taking exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> class because those taking exactly one class have no overlap with those taking exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> classes as shown in our Venn Diagram and because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> classes are subcases for finding the total number of students as we know that each student is in exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/578e7bfedba53ec0a43fdbcb8270d17899aa37a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> classes. This means that exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students took strictly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> class.\n</p><p>We can add up our equations we found to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because those equations were for subcases of having exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> class giving:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b2800c98249ab3eae01223c23c74578782107cdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4+d)+(1+b)+a=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"20\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/8/998eb15d64eb0892dccec875ffd9c23bed5d6e2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=5+a+b+d=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>From our equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/b/32bbce32e0ccae1a591ac7a2225e3b98c559562b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />, we can substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/6221281e0eab63c05adcaf37a3cb6e01188eb029.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-c$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f2f15037a372d8d68c92babeafeab8aab06884a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> giving us:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/6046c814110ca397c23a36180bfef8f95eaabf91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+9-c=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/8271d4342b38d2ab38bb626ffad8b9dae00b5e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />. We assigned <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> for the number of people taking exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> classes meaning that when we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, we find the answer. This means our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/9/839629ebf828819ef27e34dd74f00334642df97c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(C) 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"49\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>~Batmanstark\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are told that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students in all, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> take yoga, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> take bridge, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> take painting.\nRepresenting each student as a number from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we can then make a list of which classes they are taking. Students 1-10 take yoga, and students <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> take bridge. However, this means that only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students are taking bridge. To make up for it, we go back to the top of the list and start over from student <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Students <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will also take bridge giving the desired count of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> total bridge students. \n</p><p>Now, all that is left are the students who take painting. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> students who take painting, so students <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through students <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> take painting. Note that because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people take at least two classes, students <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are unable to take more than one class. This means that we must once more start over from the top. Already <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> painting slots have been filled, so students <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will also take painting. This gives a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> students (students <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) who take all three classes. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44eb511c4f725b6b8f6c6a941d77324031885652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~TheGoldenRetriever\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Overcounting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Overcounting)\">Solution 6 (Overcounting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Overcounting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22ac80e6484d593f943cc3278a4e132e9ccfe0ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 + 13 + 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. But here, every student who takes at least two classes was overcounted (included in the counts for both classes). We are given that this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> students. And every student who takes all three classes was overcounted again, as they were not only included in the count for the two mentioned earlier, but also in the count for the third class. So, we get the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/923384fa1bff9c16d0d47fc1b9913f8d22eefc31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32 - 9 - x = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"15\" /> (the actual amount of students). Solving, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/407e8baa1fb54f38c50503e5c270e9ead30f333f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~banana.bread\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B\">2017 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Pr